    "body": "open_listing_file() stores sys.stderr in the thread-local cython_errors_echo_file, but close_listing_file() only cleared the listing file, leaving the stderr reference dangling. A later warning() (e.g. the c_string_encoding notice from detect_opened_file_encoding) could then write to a stderr the caller had already closed or redirected, raising \"ValueError: I/O operation on closed file\". This surfaced as an intermittent failure of\nTestCythonUtils.test_detect_file_encoding under the parallel test harness. Clear echo_file on close so it no longer outlives the compile.",
    "closed_at": null,
