                "message": "Reset echo_file in close_listing_file() to avoid writing to a closed stderr\n\nopen_listing_file() stores sys.stderr in the thread-local\ncython_errors_echo_file, but close_listing_file() only cleared the\nlisting file, leaving the stderr reference dangling. A later warning()\n(e.g. the c_string_encoding notice from detect_opened_file_encoding)\ncould then write to a stderr the caller had already closed or\nredirected, raising \"ValueError: I/O operation on closed file\". This\nsurfaced as an intermittent failure of\nTestCythonUtils.test_detect_file_encoding under the parallel test\nharness. Clear echo_file on close so it no longer outlives the compile.",
